  "scope": "Root actually read the complete original and final proposed seven-item owner, the entire 395-line frozen derivation, the complete comparison, all twenty literal guards, both full bibliography pairs and both complete end-Programs tables, and every proposed event field. Root read both whole new programs and every output row, the complete run and primary-reading receipts, freeze/release receipts, and bounded historical-program and receiver scopes. Root actually viewed the complete published Liu--Rollenske Table1 image on printed187 and Milnor printed111--115, including complete B1--B3 proofs, B4 and the positivity proof. Milnor115 presents the free-module/colength equality as Problem3; the comparison supplies its finite-module, regular-sequence, Tor and Nakayama proof. The printed positivity theorem uses polynomial wording; the frozen derivation explicitly transports every step to the analytic gradient map. Further primary reading belongs to ii_check_a. The ambient-germ isomorphism, actual residue divisor, unit maps, full common powers and unequal component multiplicities are explicit. The final global invocation has its all-supports domain. The seven printed items and all deformation, Hessian, critical-remainder and normalization formulas are preserved. No independent credit is assigned to postrelease repairs or receiver reading, and no Paper II rendered-page credit or global defect closure is claimed.",
